Original title HET LAND VAN DE HOEDO, Jan. 1, 1948

Documenting the everyday life of Dayak Bahau upstream Mahakam river, Nederlandsch-Indië, Borneo (at present East Borneo, Indonesia). The women take care of the huts, cook food and do work on land. Men fishing with spears, hunt with poisonous blowpipe dart in the forest. There are war dances with mandau, dances performed by children and interestingly at the end appear Hudoq dancers.

The Hudoq dance is usually held every time it's finished (planting rice) in the fields every year. The meaning is, begging God's blessing so that the planted rice will produce grains that are many-fold to bring prosperity to the community.

"Het Land van de Hoedo" (Tanah Hudoq), sebuah dokumenter kehidupan penduduk Pulau Kalimantan yang dibuat pada tahun 1947.

Lokasi: Provinsi Kalimantan Timur, Kalimantan Selatan, dan Kalimantan Tengah, Indonesia
Tim Produksi: J.D. Bertel, W. Federoff, Jacques Pompe, P. Reijntjes, dan J.H. Zindler
Produksi: Multifilm Batavia.


